# Secrets and runtime state live in ~/.trinovata/, deliberately OUTSIDE this
# folder — capture-bot.env holds the Telegram BOT_TOKEN and must never be in
# Dev. These entries are belt-and-braces in case anything is ever created here
# by mistake.
*.env
.env
.env.*
!*.env.example

# Logs and state, if they ever land beside the code
*.log
*-state.json
ingest-*.log

# Node
node_modules/
package-lock.json
npm-debug.log*

# Captured payloads must never be committed. They are arbitrary forwarded
# content from the internet — treated as untrusted data everywhere else in this
# codebase, and they belong in the vault, not in source control.
inbox/
attachments/
captures/

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Worktree checkouts are duplicate copies of this repo, never content.
# Committing them is how a repo ends up tracking itself as a gitlink.
.claude/worktrees/
